==English==

===Etymology===
Possibly related to northern English or Scottish [[scunner]]: "to shrink back in fear or loathing" (Encyclopædia Britannica 1911).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈskaʊndɹəl/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/"skaUndr@l/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# one without [[honor]]; a [[villain]]

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Wikisaurus:villain]]

====Derived terms====
* [[scoundrelly]]

